##" US public transit from the FTA National Transit Database. Two sources. `transit`: monthly ridership and service for every US agency, 2002 to August 2026 (trips, service hours, recovery since 2019, the Triangle against Sun Belt peers, big vs small agencies). `ondemand_annual`: on-demand service 2022 to 2024 split into ADA paratransit and general-public on-demand (microtransit), with operating spend; use it for any microtransit, paratransit or on-demand vendor question. Playbook views answer buyer questions directly: ondemand_annual -> agencies_scaling_microtransit (who a microtransit company should call first), microtransit_market_size (the money), mostly_paratransit_agencies, paratransit_without_microtransit; transit -> does_restoring_service_bring_riders_back, triangle_vs_peer_metros, nc_agencies_below_2019, goraleigh_138_percent_check. Defaults to North Carolina on dashboards; pick any state. Sources: FTA National Transit Database on data.transportation.gov (8bui-9xvu monthly, ccvf-fykn agencies, wwdp-t4re / ekg5-frzt / uk25-sge7 / i3pw-uwab annual on-demand), public domain, downloaded 2026-10-06; row counts and 2019 / latest-12-month totals match the publisher's API (checked 2026-10-07). Known data breaks (GoRaleigh's July 2024 counts, late filers) are documented on the transit source. Fare-free sources (fare_free.malloy, added 2026-10-07): `ntd_annual_financials` (NTD Time Series 2.1 fares, cost, trips, hours by agency x mode x year 2015-2024, npsm-38gk, plus operating funding 2022-2024), `fare_policies` (hand-built list of 77 US fare-free policy episodes with a source URL each), `fare_free_events` and `fare_free_event_months` (matched event study of 61 fare changes), `fare_free_robustness`, and `agency_change` (2019 vs 2024 per agency). Use them for any fare-free, fare return or farebox question: fare_free_events -> effect_by_group, agency_change -> where_fare_free_is_cheaper, agency_change -> fare_free_vs_service_2019_2024. Cost-per-rider sources (cost_per_rider.malloy, added 2026-10-07): `ntd_cost` (the annual table in 2024 dollars with cost per trip, per passenger mile, per revenue hour and riders per hour; views national_trend, cost_by_mode_and_density), `cost_peer_gaps` (every local-bus agency 2015-2024 against its density x size peer median, with the dollars it would save at the median split into riders-per-hour and cost-per-hour levers; views savings_by_lever, biggest_gaps, nc_agencies), `cost_agency_profile` (what the cheapest quarter of each peer group does differently; quartile_profile), `network_redesign_results` (matched event study of 15 bus network redesigns; effect_by_timing), `contracting_switches` and `contracting_cross_section` (contracted vs directly operated bus), `ondemand_vs_bus` (general-public on-demand vs the same agency's bus) and `cost_savings_robustness`. Use them for any cost per rider, efficiency, contracting, microtransit cost or network redesign question. Budget-cut sources (budget_cuts.malloy, added 2026-10-07): `budget_agency` (one row per agency, 2024: operating money by source, the federal money above its own 2017-19 level = relief running out, flagged at 10%+, a validation list of systems in the 2025-26 news, the ADA paratransit share, and riders lost a year per $1M of bus or rail service cut; views in_the_news_check, biggest_gaps_big_systems, exposed_bus_agencies, gap_by_class, cut_menu_by_type, funding_mix_by_class, nc_agencies), `relief_by_year` (national_cliff 2015-2024), `relief_robustness`, `service_change_events` / `service_change_summary` / `service_change_path` (matched event study of 588 sharp service cuts and additions 2003-2026: riders move about 0.7% per 1% of bus hours cut, 0.4-0.6% per 1% added), `service_elasticity_panel`, `gtfs_frequency` and `gtfs_routes` (share of weekday bus hours on routes every 15 minutes or better, 43 agencies incl. 7 in NC, from public GTFS). Use them for any budget cut, fiscal cliff, federal relief, service cut, paratransit share or riders-per-dollar question.
## dataset { title="US Transit Ridership (NTD Monthly)" }

import { transit, STATE, AGENCY, MODE_GROUP, SIZE_BAND } from 'transit.malloy'
import { ondemand_annual } from 'ondemand.malloy'
import { ntd_annual_financials, fare_policies, fare_free_events, fare_free_event_months, fare_free_robustness, agency_change } from 'fare_free.malloy'
import { ntd_cost, cost_peer_gaps, cost_agency_profile, network_redesign_results, contracting_switches, contracting_cross_section, ondemand_vs_bus, cost_savings_robustness, MY_AGENCY } from 'cost_per_rider.malloy'
import { budget_agency, relief_by_year, relief_robustness, service_change_events, service_change_summary, service_change_path, service_elasticity_panel, gtfs_frequency, gtfs_routes, BUDGET_AGENCY } from 'budget_cuts.malloy'

export { transit, ondemand_annual, ntd_annual_financials, fare_policies, fare_free_events, fare_free_event_months, fare_free_robustness, agency_change, ntd_cost, cost_peer_gaps, cost_agency_profile, network_redesign_results, contracting_switches, contracting_cross_section, ondemand_vs_bus, cost_savings_robustness, budget_agency, relief_by_year, relief_robustness, service_change_events, service_change_summary, service_change_path, service_elasticity_panel, gtfs_frequency, gtfs_routes, STATE, AGENCY, MY_AGENCY, BUDGET_AGENCY, MODE_GROUP, SIZE_BAND }
